Thu Dec  5 14:22:18 1996  Mike Warren  <msw@cacr.caltech.edu>

	* libtree/walk.c: Made a couple of key alignment fixes that never 
	made it from johns version.

Tue Feb  6 09:53:40 1996  Mike Warren  <msw@sampson.145>

	Problems with adaptive timestep decomposition are caused by
	one proc having nobj==0 and data==NULL, which was fixed in
	johns version a few months ago.

        Wed Oct  4 12:17:15 1995  John Salmon  <johns@coho>
	* libtree/pqsort.c (pqsort): Dave P. pointed out that nobj==0,
	causes segfaults in pqsort.  The problem was really with data==NULL,
	q = data + (nobj-1)*size, which doesn't 'compare' properly with
	p = data.  The code is changed now so that it never looks at
	data[-1].  ANSI says it's ok to compare with data[nobj], but not
	with data[-1].

Mon Feb  5 14:08:44 1996  Mike Warren  <msw@sampson.145>

	* libtree/decomp.c (SetupDecomp): Avoid calling qsort if
	nobj == 0.

Thu Jan 25 12:43:12 1996  Mike Warren  <msw@sampson.145>

	* libtree/decomp.c (ClearDecomp): Allow us to clear a saved 
	decomposition.  This is necessary for the merged dark/sph code.

Wed Jan 17 11:49:40 1996  Mike Warren  <msw@sampson.145>

