Sat Dec  3 13:13:52 1994  John Salmon  <johns@mullet.anu.edu.au>

	* libmpmy/iozero.c (close0): Don't Bcast(count=-1) if
	read returns an error.  WARNING:  touching this file
	doesn't reliably trigger a re-make!

	*  libtree/pqsort.c:  The ABM termination code insists that
	you don't call ABMIamDone until you're sure the nodes you've
	sent stuff to have handled it.  This is automatic in request/reply
	operation, but it needs special care in one-way request-only
	operation.  Add two more types of handlers to pqsort to deal
	with it.  

Fri Dec  2 12:27:08 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libsw/memfile.c (PrintMemfile): Add fflush.

Thu Dec  1 09:35:07 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* libmpmy/mpmy_{nx,mpi,eui}.c: Remove MPMY_Shift_overlap.  It's in
	mpmy_generic.

	* libtree/,abm.c,mpmy_generic.c: merge with johns version, hoping
	to avoid the PollUntilDone sync problem.

	* libsw/poll.c (PollUntilDone): This is broken, and will never work
	correctly unless blocking sends are used.  We use the tacit 
	assumption that a message from proc a-->b will arrive before
	a message from a-->c-->b.  This is the source of the mysterious
	mpif failures on the SP2.  Moved to Obsolete.

	* libtree/pqsort.c (pqsort): Add a consistency check.  This will
	halt the code here if a message gets lost during pqsort, rather
	than triggering the Ninteract != gnobj error later.
	
