Tue Nov 29 09:41:48 1994  Mike Warren  (msw@sampson)

	* relerr/main_nv.c (main): do_separatefiles is now read_nfiles
	and write_nfiles.  These use the new MPMY_Nfileio technology.
	An Nfile gets the header (MPMY_SINGLO part) in the p000 file.
	A regular file can be had by concatenation of the parts.
	We can probably rip out the stuff out of SDFread that does the
	same thing. One is currently limited to reading an Nfile on the 
	same number of procs as it was written from.  This is not really 
	so bad when you consider that on the SP2 you can't get at the files
	on the local /tmp disks	from anywhere else anyway.  

	* libsw/{SDFwrite3.c,SDFwrite3a.c}: Obsolete.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_nx.c: use mpmy_io.c instead of mpmy_pario.c

	* libmpmy/iozero.c (fseekrd0): allbuf should be malloced only if
	procnum == 0.  This was a serious memory leak.
	(write0_multi): multi mode write occuring through proc 0.
	(read0_multi): multi mode read occuring through proc 0.

	* libmpmy/mpmy_{seq,eui,mpi,pvm,craypvm,sunmos,vertex}.c: include 
	mpmy_io.c instead of mpmy_unixio.c

	* libmpmy/mpmy_io.c: New IO model.  Should work correctly on
	anything that uses a unix-like open, read, write, etc.  Writes
	are serial from proc 0, so there should be no nfs problem. The 
	special collective modes (which have not been implemented in
	this model) may be somewhat faster on the paragon, and certainly
	faster on the cm5.  Some of the libSDF stuff can be cleaned up
	after this proves to be stable.

